# Substituted by `git archive` (which is what GitHub's source tarballs are),
# so a build from a downloaded tarball can still identify itself. With no .git
# directory, extra_script.py finds no metadata and config.h falls back to
# FW_VERSION_FALLBACK; this line gives the tarball the real describe output
# instead.
#
# Only `git archive` substitutes it. In a working clone the file below keeps
# the literal $Format:...$ text, which is why extra_script.py prefers calling
# git directly and treats this as the fallback path.
.tarball-version export-subst
